Description: deploy a service from an Ansible playbook catalogue
 ansible-temple reads a Git repository laid out as a playbook catalogue:
 manifest.json at the root, and playbooks/<id>/info.json plus main.yml
 for each service. It lists those services in the terminal and runs
 ansible-playbook locally for the one you choose.
 .
 The reference catalogue deploys stacks such as MariaDB, Redis, and
 WordPress. Any other repository with the same layout can be used.
 The repository address is shown before the playbook runs.
